        passage: "Early mornings are not my favourite part of the day. I would love a lie-in, but my life as a university student means I usually have to get out of bed early. A quick shower comes first, and then I put on casual, comfortable clothes, because I run errands during the day. Breakfast matters to me: a balanced one gives me energy and helps me concentrate. While I eat, I set goals, think about how to manage my time and plan the rest of the day. Just before I leave home, I check my messages and reply to them. Exercise is something else I would like to do every day, for example at the gym or by jogging, but I am often too busy. That is why I walk to university. The walk takes about twenty minutes and counts as light exercise. At university I attend lectures, listen to my professors and highlight valuable information about different subjects. After classes I participate in social events and meetings, which help me build the social and academic skills I will need in the future. Once I am home, I change my clothes, relax on the sofa for an hour and do some housework. Then I study for two hours. At night I set my alarm and go to bed early.",
