        passage: "Technology now plays a big part in education. It helps students to grasp their lessons, practise more and get better at what they study. Interactive whiteboards and online platforms are common in schools in many countries, because they make learning more interesting. Türkiye has joined this trend with a national project called Digital Transformation in Education, which gives learners and teachers new ways of working. Its online platforms contain lessons and materials that experts have prepared. Students watch videos, complete exercises and work at a speed that suits them. This makes it easier to spot their weak points and improve them one at a time. Someone who struggles with grammar, for example, can choose grammar videos and quizzes. Teachers are part of the plan as well. The project helps them learn new methods and techniques, develop their professional skills and feel more confident with digital tools in class. Through the platforms, teachers can also look up extra materials and check how well their students are progressing. The main aim is to improve the quality of education and to give every student a fair chance to succeed. By bringing technology into the classroom, Türkiye hopes to prepare young people for the future and to help teachers give lessons that work better.",
